    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Green & Clean Nairobi — Executive RAG Chatbot (Anthropic + n8n)\n\n**Setup (3 credentials + 1 ID):**\n1. **Anthropic** — *Header Auth* credential named `Anthropic API`; header **Name** `x-api-key`, **Value** your `sk-ant-...` key. Attach to nodes 3 & 10.\n2. **Postgres** — attach to `5a`; edit the table name if not `green_clean_reports`.\n3. **Google Sheets** — attach OAuth2 to `5b`; set the **documentId** to your Sheet ID.\n\nOpen the **Chat** tab and ask anything in the catalog below.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 470,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "c4549081-0ca4-4023-9682-7bc2627b339b",
      "name": "Sticky Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -512,
        -736
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Models (edit in `1. Init & Load Memory`)\nInterpretation: `claude-haiku-4-5` · Synthesis: `claude-sonnet-4-6`.\nIf you switch synthesis to `claude-sonnet-5`, remove the `temperature` line in `9. Build Synthesis Request`.",
        "height": 170,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "93680ca6-53f7-40e8-97ce-46ef4e51adbe",
      "name": "Sticky Models",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        16,
        -720
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### What it can now answer (any column)\n**Metrics:** waste loads, loads remaining, staff, attendees, trees, seedlings, bins (total/emptied), trucks, arrests, report counts.\n**Rates:** collection completion, data-quality confirmation, photo-evidence completeness, night surveillance, arrests.\n**Ratios:** bins emptied ÷ total, loads remaining ÷ collected.\n**Breakdowns:** by subcounty, ward, month, activity, incident type, vehicle, who collects (NCCG/contractor/CBO), tree type, sensitization type, flood severity/cause, drainage status, obstruction type/ownership, partners, most-lacking resources.\n**Ops:** rank, sum, avg, min/max, trend, compare, distribution.\n**Time:** understands 'last month', 'this week', 'past 30 days', 'March 2026', '3rd March', or a date range — resolved against today, then filtered.\n\n_Try:_ \"Which subcounty collected the most waste?\" · \"Breakdown of incidents by type\" · \"What share of collections were completed?\" · \"Who collects more, NCCG or contractors?\" · \"Which resources are most lacking?\" · \"Trees planted trend\" · \"Flooding by severity\".",
        "height": 186,
        "width": 716,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "04d94fa0-25db-4347-ab6a-727accab70ea",
      "name": "Sticky Capabilities",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1056,
        -688
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Dual-source + automatic fallback\nBoth sources run with *Continue on Error*. `6. Resolve` uses whichever returned data; if both do, it follows `config.sourcePreference`.\n\n⚠️ If Postgres and the Sheet hold the **same** records, set `sourcePreference` to `postgres` or `googlesheets` (not `merge`) to avoid double counting.",
        "height": 80,
        "width": 360,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "10281799-fc56-4277-94a1-3f2df71831cb",
      "name": "Sticky Fallback",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        592,
        -640
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Math firewall + validator\n`7. Math Engine` does ALL arithmetic in JS across the full metric registry and tags it `pre_computed`. The LLM only writes prose from those ground-truth numbers. `11. Validate` re-checks the headline figure (`math.primary`) and corrects drift.",
        "height": 184,
        "width": 548,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "32baefab-2c98-44b1-8377-a8a1db61af35",
      "name": "Sticky Firewall",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
